# AGENTS.md — CurrentJS Application

This is a **CurrentJS** application — a TypeScript web app generated from YAML configuration files using the `@currentjs/gen` CLI.

## Workflow

YAML is the source of truth. The recommended workflow:

1. **Install AI skills** (first time only):
   ```
   currentjs ai
   ```

2. **Create or modify modules** using the `/current-create-module` skill:
   > /current-create-module I need a Blog module with posts that have title, content, and status. Public read, authenticated create, owner/admin edit and delete.

   The more detailed description is the best. The AI will scaffold the module, write YAML, generate TypeScript, implement custom logic, and commit.

3. For subsequent changes, describe what you need in natural language — the skill handles YAML updates, regeneration, and commits.

### Manual Workflow (alternative)

```
currentjs create module Blog        # scaffold module directory + starter YAML
# edit src/modules/Blog/blog.yaml   # define models, routes, actions, permissions
currentjs generate Blog             # generate TypeScript from YAML
# optionally customize generated code
currentjs commit                    # preserve manual edits across regeneration
```

## Key Commands

| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `currentjs create module <Name>` | Scaffold a new module |
| `currentjs generate [module]` | Generate TypeScript from YAML configs |
| `currentjs commit [files...]` | Preserve manual edits across regeneration |
| `currentjs diff [module]` | Show generated vs current code differences |
| `currentjs migrate commit` | Generate SQL migration from model changes |
| `currentjs migrate push` | Apply pending migrations to database |
| `currentjs ai` | Install/update AI skills |

## Project Structure

```
app.yaml                        # App-level config (do not edit manually)
src/
├── app.ts                      # Server entry + DI wiring (auto-managed section)
├── system.ts                   # Env loading, decorators
├── common/ui/templates/        # Layout + error templates
└── modules/<ModuleName>/
    ├── <name>.yaml             # Module config (source of truth)
    ├── domain/entities/        # Entity classes
    ├── application/services/   # Business logic
    ├── application/dto/        # Input/output DTOs
    ├── infrastructure/
    │   ├── controllers/        # API + Web controllers
    │   └── stores/             # Database access
    └── views/                  # HTML templates
```

## Important Rules

- **YAML drives generation.** Edit YAML, then `currentjs generate`. Don't hand-edit generated files without committing.
- **Auto-generated fields:** `id`, `ownerId`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `deletedAt` are added automatically — never define them in YAML.
- **`currentjs commit`** saves manual edits so they survive regeneration. Do not make early commits – it will pollute the registry.
- **`src/app.ts`** has marker comments (`// currentjs:controllers:start` / `end`) — the generator manages that section automatically.
- **Custom business logic** goes in Service methods, referenced from YAML as `service:methodName` handlers.
